WEBVTT

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.380
This is Sakuragi Park.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:28.130
As usual, Satoshi and Go
are looking after the Pokémon, when...

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.470
Oh, Koharu.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.840
What’re you doing?

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.600
Dad asked me to take photos
of the Pokémon here.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.730
Oh, the regularly scheduled photos.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.480
We take those sometimes, too.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.560
Huh, is that so?

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.900
What should I snap next?

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.570
You want to guide me,
Wanpachi?

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.780
Ooh, there’s a trusty pal!

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:59.080
Let’s see where he’s going, Go!

00:00:59.080 --> 00:00:59.910
Yeah!

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.980
Oh, Wanpachi...

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.940
He’s like a big brother to everyone.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.410
Sarunori?
Where have you been?

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.700
Oh, you lost your stick?!

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.820
Thank you, Wanpachi!

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:09.480
He really is everyone’s big bro!

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.320
Great work, Wanpachi!

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.330
What’s wrong?

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.790
All right!
Let’s follow Wanpachi!

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:09.060
Kaiross?

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:10.610
What’s she doing?

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:12.440
She doesn’t look too happy...

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.700
It’s Dredear and Himenka.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.200
What a sweet scent!

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.540
Who’s this?

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.220
<i>Heracross?</i>

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.340
<i>Oh, dear...</i>

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.400
Heracross got seduced
by Dredear’s sweet scent.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.900
That’s happened before,
hasn’t it?

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.150
Yeah.

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.150
Don’t worry about it, Kaiross.

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.240
He’ll be back to normal
before long.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:09.330
Wanpachi?
Where are you going?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.640
Huh? Hiyape?

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:40.190
Is he trying to say,
“Wake up!”?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:10.060
Isn’t that nice, Kaiross?

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:22.610
Ah!

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:23.490
Not again!

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:34.080
Are they going to be okay?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.170
They’ll make up
before long, yeah.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:37.630
Totally.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.590
It’s Koratta!

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:43.260
Now what?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:03.150
They’re fighting!

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.160
Why are you fighting?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.410
Yeah, why?

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:14.410
You need to get along!

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.540
Golugh, what happened?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:23.800
Poppo, Koratta, and the others
are usually playing here...

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:26.220
Did the Rock Pokémon
take their space?

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:30.390
They don’t look like
they’ll budge, either.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:32.180
What a mess...

00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:35.020
Wanpachi?

00:07:35.020 --> 00:07:36.270
Again?!

00:07:36.270 --> 00:07:38.190
Did you think of something?

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.820
Isn’t this...?

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:50.030
That’s it!

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.450
This is where the Rock Pokémon
usually play!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.040
But the water...

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:00.790
What’s that noise?!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.840
It’s hurting my ears!

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.010
Hagigishiri!

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.850
Was Hagigishiri
making that noise just now?

00:08:15.850 --> 00:08:18.600
I wonder if it’s annoyed
by the dirty water...

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:23.400
Of course...
That <i>would</i> send the Rock Pokémon running.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.030
Stop it, Hagigishiri!

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.860
We have to do something...!

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:30.740
But what can we do?

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:34.790
It’s too loud!
I can’t think!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:37.250
Wanpachi?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.470
Vibrava!

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:54.680
It couldn’t be...

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.510
You’re kidding!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.510
What?!

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:56.520
Supersonic Waves!

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.400
It’s so loud!

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:11.200
Huh?

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.740
The noise is gone.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:13.870
But how?

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:20.750
Vibrava’s Supersonic Waves and Hagigishiri’s gnashing
might be canceling each other out.

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.880
Can that really happen?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:28.170
When a wave combines
with its exact opposite, the sound vanishes.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:31.050
Like positive and negative
summing to make zero.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.390
Wow!
The power of science is amazing!

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.720
Great job, Wanpachi!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:41.270
But we can’t leave things like this.

00:09:42.350 --> 00:09:44.770
We have to do something
about the polluted water!

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:47.530
Yeah.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.200
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:12.050
You okay, Pikachu?

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:15.390
It’s all slimy!

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:17.350
Look, Satoshi!

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:20.390
There’s more all over!

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.480
What is it, Wanpachi?

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.400
Namakobushi?

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:38.620
Is this slimy stuff
what polluted the river?

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:39.990
No, it couldn’t be.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:44.670
Namakobushi’s slime is a mucus
that covers its body, so it wouldn’t pollute the water.

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:49.670
It probably just fled
from the polluted river, too.

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:52.590
Let’s investigate some more!

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:53.590
Yeah!

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.060
That came from where Golugh is!

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.980
They’re still going at it...

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.110
Not just that...
It’s gotten <i>worse.</i>

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.920
They’ve settled down for now...

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.090
But we have to find the cause,
and quick!

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.460
Let’s go upstream!

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.460
Yeah!

00:11:43.810 --> 00:11:46.730
Vibrava’s looking pretty tired!

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:47.810
Let’s hurry!

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:48.850
Yeah!

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:50.810
Namakobushi!

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:53.190
Just hold on a little longer!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:55.570
We’ve gotta hurry!

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:56.070
Yeah!

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:08.870
In the end,
we didn’t find anything...

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.420
There wasn’t a pile of trash
or anything...

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:15.300
And it doesn’t look like
the Poison-type Pokémon did it, either...

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.760
Hmm...

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:19.800
Wanpachi?

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.800
Did he find something?

00:12:36.490 --> 00:12:38.400
Betobeta!

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.950
Why is it here?

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.580
So that’s what
polluted the water!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.870
Hey! Come outta there,
Betobeta!

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.370
Looks like it’s not budging...

00:13:03.350 --> 00:13:05.350
All right!
It came out!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:06.850
Sorry.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:09.770
The water gets polluted
if you stay there.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.440
Where did Betobeta live originally?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:17.230
It used to be in a cave.

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:17.990
Yeah.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.990
Let’s take it back there.

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:23.950
Is this the place?

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:24.950
Yeah.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.750
Betobeta likes trash and sludge,

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:31.960
so it was living here
where it wouldn’t trouble anyone.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:33.420
“Kero”?

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.300
Keromatsu?!

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.470
Why is Keromatsu here?

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:47.810
Maybe...

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:53.400
Betobeta gave its home to Keromatsu,
since it’s new here...

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.610
So that’s what happened!

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:57.900
You’re really kind, Betobeta.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.410
Oh, but...

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:06.370
Where will Betobeta live, then?

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:11.290
Right... We can’t let it go
back to the waterfall...

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:12.370
I know!

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:16.420
We can all build a new home
for Betobeta, together!

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.420
Yeah!

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:23.010
All right! You all ready?

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:28.140
We’re counting on all of you!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.640
Hey, you still not ready? C’mon, hurry up!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.150
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:37.900
I’ll show you this wide mysterious world

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:40.530
And skip the slow send-off

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:43.200
Be it through fire or through water

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:45.820
I’m fumbling blindly through the days

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:50.620
When I don’t even know what the next second will bring

00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:52.120
Now if we just put some water in,
it’ll be finished!

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.670
What’s that?

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.630
On 1, 2, 3, leap out!

00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:07.220
Out of the miserable days of tears,

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:09.810
and out of your Ball

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:13.560
“Where should we go?”, you ask?

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.560
Suicune...

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:16.600
The answer’s gotta be “Everywhere!”

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:20.900
No time (No time!) to catch your breath! Try! (Try!)

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:22.150
Why don’t we go?

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:24.820
1. Leap the language barrier

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:28.280
2. And go beyond the borders

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:28.280
Rain Prayer?

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:31.330
to discover a new you

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:34.870
If I were to collapse, to fall to my knees

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:37.710
I’ll do what I always did

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:40.290
Straighten my shadow out, like the setting sun

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:43.010
even though I may be taller now

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:45.550
Let’s go! It’s only after the rain...

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.260
Let’s go! ...that you see a rainbow in clear skies

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:52.510
I’ve known that since that day

00:15:55.520 --> 00:15:57.270
Satoshi, look!

00:16:01.650 --> 00:16:06.530
Have you, have you perhaps maybe

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:10.490
grown up without me noticing?

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:14.290
In the right-side pocket

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:16.960
of your dusty old clothes

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:19.580
You left the handheld adventure

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.040
that was everything to us

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:24.840
The memories from those days

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:28.550
are now looking for you!

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:33.430
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:40.190
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:46.280
So let’s go somewhere! Take me somewhere, anywhere!

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:50.530
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.820
Let’s have a fight!

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:54.450
1. Once the battle’s done

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:56.540
2. And we’re laughing or crying

00:16:56.540 --> 00:17:00.960
On 3, let’s be friends!

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.960
What a gentle rain...

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:02.920
Yeah.

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:07.260
Any day and every day, that’s always been my rule

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:12.640
With this unpredictable, unfathomable world awaiting

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:15.220
Let’s go! Every time you trip and fall

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.560
Let’s go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.140
Okay, Betobeta!

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:19.560
This is your new home!

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:21.270
I choose you!

00:18:29.300 --> 00:18:33.130
Suicune must’ve seen
just how hard Wanpachi was working.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.050
Yeah!

00:18:34.050 --> 00:18:37.100
Sometimes,
Pokémon just really amaze you.

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.600
Even if they’re far apart...

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:49.360
The stronger their feelings are,
the closer they’re connected.

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:53.150
Feelings can get through to them.
Your feelings, too, Go.

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:56.410
Well, I can hope.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.500
See you, Suicune.

00:20:01.600 --> 00:20:03.060
It looks really happy!

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:11.770
The Rock Pokémon
got to go back home, too.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:17.530
Everyone’s all back to normal.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.820
Ah, what a relief!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.040
Thanks for all your work,
Wanpachi!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:32.210
Wanpachi played a big role in helping
the Pokémon of Sakuragi Park.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:37.800
They even saw Suicune for the first time in a while.
What a wonderful day!

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:43.050
That’s it for today’s chores!

00:20:45.100 --> 00:20:47.730
Koharu,
did you get some good photos?

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.390
Yes, they’re great!

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:52.020
I snapped lots of shots
of Wanpachi working hard, too!

00:20:57.570 --> 00:21:00.110
An official battle date and time
has been set.

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:03.330
A Masters Eight Promotion Match.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:07.250
Your opponent is Competitor Kibana,
ranked 8th.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.460
Mr. Kibana, huh?

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:12.000
A Promotion Match?

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:17.340
If Competitor Satoshi wins this battle,
their rankings will be swapped,

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:23.720
and he will join the renowned Masters Eight,
the eight strongest in the Pokémon World Championships.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.140
Huh...

00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:26.890
That’s incredible, Satoshi!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.270
The day’s finally come.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:31.350
Yeah!

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:39.610
Satoshi blazes with fighting spirit for his battle
against Kibana. How will their battle end?!

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:09.660
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:11.580 --> 00:23:15.920
Satoshi is currently ranked 9th
in the Pokémon World Championships!

00:23:15.920 --> 00:23:18.380
I’m finally gonna have my Masters Eight
Promotion Match!

00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:20.460
You’re facing Mr. Kibana, right?

00:23:22.050 --> 00:23:25.300
If we’re gonna win, Lucario,
we’ve gotta get stronger!

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.050
And to do that...

00:23:27.050 --> 00:23:29.550
Let’s go and see Gekkouga!

00:23:29.550 --> 00:23:31.560
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:34.850
Lucario and Gekkouga!
The Aura of Destiny!!
